  <title>8.2.3: Self Check</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02109</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.2.3: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f295ef05-ebd3-41dd-a64c-400702358549</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <note class="self-check"><para>The expressions \(s(60 − 12s)\) and \(-12s^2 + 60s\) define the same function. A soap bubble machine can launch many soap bubbles into the air before they begin to pop. The function given models the number of soap bubbles floating in the air in \(s\) seconds.</para>
<para>According to the function, how many seconds have passed before all of the bubbles have been made and also popped?</para></note>
</content>
</document>
